{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## ALL THREE TEST-REPAIR CHANGES ARE MERGED\n\n    4bbbdd991  5200: pin the three repaired J11 oracles          (1279)\n    a1037d020  5200: make three J11 live cells able to fail      (1280)\n    b6916709f  5200: add the missing row 12 outbound cell        (1283)\n\nEach earned `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`; confirmed against `gerrit/main`, not the GitHub mirror.\n1283 needed TWO rebases before CI would pass — both times the stale-base trap with a different script\n(`check_config_reads.py`, then `probe_rebar.py` in `golden-path`), and I wasted one cycle treating the\nsecond as a flake before the identical repeat showed it was structural. Rule now recorded in the session\nlog: on a CI failure naming a missing file under `scripts/`, REBASE — do not recheck.\n\nSo criterion 11's three gaps are closed or recorded: **row 1 outbound BUILT**, **row 12 outbound BUILT**,\nand **row 14 inbound's oracle amended** because the AC prescribed an entry that can never fire (snapshot\nentries carry no `jira_key` FIELD, so `differ.py:641-651` always reads falsy). The `08-assign` vacuity is\ngone, and the pagination precondition no longer measures itself with the code under test.\n\n### WHAT REMAINS BEFORE THIS TICKET CAN CLOSE\n\nA FRESH HARNESS RUN. The last one (30784592232) predates all three of these merges, so the live suite has\nnever executed with the repaired cells — it collected 56 then and collects **58** now. Do not tick the\nharness-dependent ACs off the old run.\n\nExpect, on the next run:\n * `test_outbound_unassign_round_trips` GREEN (751e already verified live).\n * `test_inbound_delete_link_round_trips` **still RED** until 2b16's arbitration fix lands — its merged fix\n   does not work; see 2b16's ticket. **Do not invert it.**\n * `test_inbound_clear_parent_round_trips` may report `SETUP FAILED` rather than green: DC REFUSES to null a\n   sub-task's `fields.parent` (HTTP 400 \"data was not an object\"). That is a PLATFORM finding, which is\n   exactly what the cell was built to report distinctly.\n * `test_outbound_clear_parent_round_trips` RED — that is [rebar:39c1-2a32-b564-4b4b], now confirmed live.\n * The new row-1-outbound cell is the one to watch: its author flagged its SETUP as the likeliest first\n   failure (no prior cell exercises an outbound create), and it fails loudly at the `get_jira_key`\n   assertion saying the problem is upstream of the provenance markers.\n\nThe 18 ACs have already been independently verified and the results are recorded above; the outstanding\nwork is the run, not the analysis."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785770109875363001,"uuid":"cb6d1696-8464-486d-8477-2c6c26d8f3c8"}